{
  "borough": "Harrow",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height:normal&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:&amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;,sans-serif&quot;&gt;The proposal, by reason or of insufficient Gross Internal floor Area (GIA) together with inadequate living space for the first floor flat would provide an overall cramped and substandard quality of living accommodation, to the detriment of the residential amenities of the existing and future occupiers of the unit, contrary to policies DM1 and DM 26 of the Harrow Development Management Policies Local Plan (2013).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height:normal&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:&amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;,sans-serif&quot;&gt;The kitchen areas of the new unit would be provided with unsatisfactory levels of natural light and outlook. The proposed development would therefore give rise to substandard and poor quality accommodation to the detriment of the residential amenities of the future occupiers of the unit contrary to policies D3 D (7) and D6 D of The London Plan (2021), policies DM1 C and DM1 D (f) of the Harrow Development Management Policies Local Plan (2013), the Mayor of London Housing Supplementary Planning Guidance (2016), Department for Communities and Local Government Technical Housing Standards – Nationally Described Space Standards (2015), and the adopted Supplementary Planning Documents Residential Design Guide (2010).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
